UPDATE questions SET wrong = '{"1": "Percentage (or fractional) uncertainty is used to judge accuracy, not precision.", "2": "The size of the quantity affects the percentage uncertainty, which relates to accuracy. Precision depends on the instrument.", "3": "Averaging readings can reduce random error, but precision is set by the least count of the instrument."}', updated_at = unixepoch() * 1000 WHERE id = 'PHY-0485';
UPDATE questions SET wrong = '{"0": "Force and energy are derived quantities. Their dimensions, [MLT⁻²] and [ML²T⁻²], are built from M, L and T.", "2": "Luminous intensity and amount of substance are SI base quantities, but the five dimensions used here are current and temperature instead.", "3": "Velocity, acceleration and force are derived quantities whose dimensions come from M, L and T."}', updated_at = unixepoch() * 1000 WHERE id = 'PHY-0493';
UPDATE questions SET wrong = '{"0": "Equations of motion can be checked this way. For example, S = ½at² is dimensionally consistent: both sides are [L].", "1": "Dimensions describe the nature of a quantity, not its unit system, so the method works with any consistent units.", "3": "The opposite is true. The method can say an equation is wrong, but it cannot identify which term is wrong."}', updated_at = unixepoch() * 1000 WHERE id = 'PHY-0502';
UPDATE questions SET wrong = '{"0": "The convention ties the positive direction to the initial velocity, not always to upward.", "1": "If all quantities were positive, a retardation would wrongly be treated as speeding the body up.", "2": "An acceleration opposite to the initial velocity, a retardation, must be negative, so acceleration is not always positive."}', updated_at = unixepoch() * 1000 WHERE id = 'PHY-0530';
UPDATE questions SET wrong = '{"0": "β⁺ decay changes a proton into a neutron, raising N/Z. It happens when the N/Z ratio is too small.", "2": "A neutrino is never emitted on its own in decay. It always comes with a β particle.", "3": "Capturing an electron turns a proton into a neutron, which raises N/Z even further. It suits nuclides with too few neutrons."}', updated_at = unixepoch() * 1000 WHERE id = 'PHY-1032';
